<title>TURKEY: TABLE-TURKISH MIGROS H1 NET PROFIT RISES.</title>
<headline>TABLE-TURKISH MIGROS H1 NET PROFIT RISES.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>				    H1 1997	   H1 1996</p>
<p>				    -------	   -------</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira) 1,408.81  vs   1,033.69</p>
<p>    Net Profit		  1,331.32  vs     558.19</p>
<p>    Net sales		  40,762.43  vs  17,786.18</p>
<p>    Operating profit	    599.26  vs	78.61 loss</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	1,441.83  vs     905.26</p>
<p>    Interest paid		   0     vs	 0</p>
<p>    Total debts		15,985.98  vs   6,309.16</p>
<p>    Equity			4,849.78  vs   2,190.08</p>
<p>    Capital			 945.00  vs     540.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's leading supermarket chain Migros Turk T.A.S. is owned 55.11 percent by Temel Ticaret, an affiliate of Koc Holding, one of Turkey's leading industrial conglomerates.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>Migros recently announced that it aimed to raise the number of markets in Turkey by 53 to 177 and boost turnover to more than 100 trillion lira by end-1997.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
